  "id": "Compound::DB01069 - Gene::1129",
  "verbalization": "Promethazine is implicated in the interaction with Hrh4, which participates in multiple receptor activity pathways, including G-protein coupled acetylcholine receptor activity and neurotransmitter receptor activity. These pathways are ultimately linked to Chrm2, a receptor involved in acetylcholine signaling. The evidence suggests that Promethazine may modulate Chrm2 through Hrh4, potentially by influencing the activity of G-protein coupled receptors. The varying scores across the paths indicate a consistent but nuanced relationship, with Hrh4 acting as a central mediator in the interaction between Promethazine and Chrm2. The overlapping pathways highlight a possible role for Hrh4 in linking Promethazine to Chrm2, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
